faqTitle: How does
faqTitleEm: Chayce help?
faqs:
- q: How does Chayce actually help me move?
  a: 'We act as your single point of contact for the whole move: sorting and packing, estate agent liaison, removals, utility transfers and settling into your new home. You tell us where you&rsquo;re at, and we take over from there.'
- q: Do I need to have sold my house first?
  a: No. We can step in at any stage, whether you&rsquo;re still deciding, mid-sale, or already holding keys to a new home.
- q: What if I only need help with one part of the move?
  a: That&rsquo;s fine. Support ranges from focused help with a single stage to a fully managed, white-glove move. You pick the level that fits.
- q: Can you help a parent or family member, not just me?
  a: Yes. We work directly with the person moving, and just as often with the son, daughter or family member helping to arrange it, wherever they happen to be.
- q: How is Chayce different from a normal removals company?
  a: We&rsquo;re a full relocation partner, not just a removal firm, managing everything from home sorting and staging through to moving day and support once you&rsquo;re settled.
- q: Will I have the same coordinator the whole way through?
  a: Yes. The same coordinator stays with you from your first conversation through to settling in. You&rsquo;re not handed off to someone new partway through.
- q: What happens if my moving date changes partway through?
  a: Your plan is built to flex. If dates shift, your coordinator adjusts bookings and timelines around the new date rather than starting again.
- q: How quickly can things move once I decide to go ahead?
  a: As quickly as you need. The plan is built around your timeline and pace, not a fixed template.
